       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you've confirmed it. But 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum dose, and the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit, isn't a clinical reason that would make that dose safe. The risk of lactic acidosis is real, and a normal kidney function doesn't remove it.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release. I can add a note that titration is planned.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose.** One option is 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up.\n- **Enter a different dose you specify,** as long as it's within labeled limits.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please take it through pharmacy or your institution's override process. Then the order can be entered with that approval documented.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it now so it's in place before evening rounds."
